  ☐ Implement physically motivated volumetric clouds integrated with the sky.
    - Approved proposal: docs/PBR.VolumetricClouds.Proposal.md (2026-10-16), archived at e87de94d.
      Its implementation checklist docs/PBR.VolumetricClouds.todo is archived at the same commit;
      read both with git show <commit>:<path>. Current qualification is in PBR.CloudRealtime.todo.
      User visual/performance acceptance and the recorded reflection dependency remain open.
    - Realtime work tasklist: docs/PBR.CloudRealtime.todo; reconcile
      sampling, self-lighting, termination, reconstruction, atmosphere and acceleration costs there.
      Its Phase 8 evaluates repeated shading work and cloud-internal lighting reuse at preserved
      initial settings. Subphases 8.1–8.4 supply segmented attenuation, depth-correct transmission
      filtering, bounded generation allocation and transported per-source projection orientation;
      measured costs, rejected area sampling and
      contention are recorded in that checklist, with final acceptance still open. Cache
      projection and source validity remain same-frame. Planned subphases 8.5/8.6 replace the
      segmented atlas and per-neighbor transmission filtering with a compact front-depth/mean-
      extinction/maximum-optical-depth record, sampled once with hardware parameter filtering.
      This deliberately changes the approximation to reduce repeated lookup cost; measured
      comparisons and final visual/performance acceptance remain required. Planned subphase 8.7
      budgets primary samples over the clipped cloud-layer intersection, including measured selection
      of the budget distance to prevent unintended work increases and explicit uncertified-bound fallback.
      Quarter tracing is
      now the default by explicit user direction; explicit Half remains supported. Phase 9 moves perturbation octaves to
      a static volumetric noise texture; Phase 10 improves temporal retention and evaluates LumOn
      reprojection/invalidation reuse. Phase 11 retains final qualification.
      Implementation phases use cached incremental builds, affected-contract checks and existing
      baseline evidence. Full baseline reproduction and canonical release/package verification are
      final-qualification work in Phase 11, not repeated completion gates for each increment; follow
      the validation scope in PBR.CloudRealtime.todo / Execution and evidence.
      External cast-shadow deferral is unchanged.
    - Define bounded 3D cloud density, altitude/weather controls, wind and volume lighting. Evaluate
      ray marching, light transmittance and a controlled multiple-scattering approximation.
    - Defer shadows cast by clouds until virtual shadow maps are implemented; retain cloud-volume self-shadowing.
    - Integrate cloud/atmosphere ordering, sun occlusion and environment lighting in
      both PBR modes. Support ground, inside-cloud and above-cloud views without depth-order errors.
    - Add quality-scaled resolution/steps, empty-space skipping and temporal reconstruction where
      useful; invalidate history correctly on movement, weather changes and lighting transitions.
    - Define replacement of vanilla clouds and clean disable/reload behavior. Validate thin/thick
      clouds, moving sun, weather, disocclusion, water reflections and fog; measure GPU and memory cost.

