      docs/PBR.CloudHierarchy.Proposal.md and docs/PBR.CloudHierarchy.todo. Current architecture:
      docs/PBR.Clouds.md; remaining sampling/performance work: docs/PBR.CloudRealtime.todo.
      Native leaves retain owned coarse min/max height summaries.
    - Reduced tracing uses certified root-height rejection with direct native-support fallback.
      Primary root misses reject whole rays without changing the sample span/count/jitter; solar/lunar
      roots skip proven-empty scheduled positions. Primary and retained secondary transport have no
      column DDA or tree descent; cache generation uses a bounded native-support walk on short chords.
      Primary sampling is independent of summary availability. Archived automated integration qualification
      applies to its recorded candidate; total GPU benefit and user-run
      live acceptance remain open, so this parent item is not complete.

  ✔ Compact volumetric cloud intermediates and reconstruct native OIT accumulation bins at resolve. @done(26-10-17)
    - Implementation uses three named RGBA32F images per set, with physical radiance/transmission,
      bucket transmissions and unchanged depth metadata. Resolve reconstructs products per admitted
      tap before spatial interpolation to retain neighboring color/coverage covariance; temporal
      history filters the compact factors. Native OIT outputs and sampling budgets remain unchanged.
    - Automated qualification: 94 unique passing checks across the final targeted and qualification
      receipts. Paired 512x512 synthetic three-pass GPU medians improved by about 0.05 ms in all
      three measured scenes (11-24%); this is not whole-game frame-time or other-resolution proof.
      Evidence: artifacts/compact-cloud-validation/validation.md. User confirmed the packaged build's
      cloud edges, moving/lighting transitions and overlapping transparency look acceptable (2026-10-17).
    - Store integrated physical RGB radiance and overall transmission, three bucket transmissions,
      and existing depth metadata instead of three separately accumulated RGBA bucket textures.
      A uniform array-compatible layout uses three RGBA32F layers per trace/history block:
      radiance/transmission, bucket transmissions/spare, and depth metadata (48 versus 80 bytes
      per reduced pixel per block). Preserve final native OIT outputs, weighting and scene encoding.
    - Reconstruct each bucket as vec4(radiance, 1 - transmission) * (1 - bucketTransmission).
      Evaluate the changed temporal clamping and spatial filtering: filtering factors separately
      does not generally equal filtering their products. Compare against the existing path at cloud
      edges, lighting/weather transitions, disocclusions and overlapping transparent geometry.
    - Use subagent-run focused correctness tests and user-run visual comparisons before adoption.
      Measure matched end-to-end cloud GPU cost, including trace, temporal and resolve; distinguish
      storage/fetch reductions from measured speedup and retain existing traversal/lighting quality.

  ☑ Consolidate volumetric cloud trace and temporal history storage into one Texture2DArray.
    - Build on the validated compact cloud-payload task above: allocate nine RGBA32F layers as
      three independent three-layer blocks for current trace, previous history and next history.
      Use rotating block indices and advance roles only after successful frame submission/history
      commit. Preserve invalidation on skipped/failed frames and keep PMJ sampling indices independent.
    - Expose disjoint block texture views so sampled images exclude the attached write block;
      shader layer offsets alone must not be used to establish framebuffer-feedback safety.
      Reuse existing immutable array storage, texture views, layer attachments and typed bindings.
    - Precreate block framebuffer attachments and integrate alias/resource declarations with the
      existing PSO system. Name the array and views; preserve resize/reload/disposal ownership,
      exception-safe allocation, depth rejection and the final native OIT output contract.
    - Verify block rotation, read/write separation, history invalidation and resource retirement
      with subagent-run focused GPU tests against equivalent separate-texture storage. Compare
      outputs and capture bindings; measure any speedup rather than inferring it from object count.
    - Verified: 162 unique passing generator/cloud/shared GPU cases; bit-exact separate-storage
      comparisons, actual rotating bindings, interrupted-submission recovery and resource retirement.
      Canonical Release package rebuilt. No speedup claim or measurement is attached to this change.
      Evidence: ../artifacts/array-cloud-validation/validation.md.

